Output:  342215This algorithm for answering queries with Sparse Table works in O(k), which is O(log(n)) because we choose minimal k such that 2^k+1 > n.Time complexity of sparse table construction : Outer loop runs in O(k), inner loop runs in O(n). Thus, in total we get O(n * k) = O(n * log(n)) Auxiliary Space: O(n*k), since n*k extra space has been taken.
